{#-
Extractors:
  - facts: AnchorExtractor("<FACTS>", "</FACTS>")
-#}
{% set summary_target = "chapter "+to_str(num_extra_context+1) %}
{% if extra_context -%}
<|SECTION:PREVIOUS CHAPTERS|>
{% for chapter_summary in extra_context %}
## Chapter {{ loop.index }}
{{ chapter_summary }}

{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif -%}
{% if previous_facts -%}
<|SECTION:KNOWN FACTS|>
Facts already recorded from earlier chapters. Reference an id in "supersedes" when a new fact replaces one of these.
Record age is display metadata, not part of the fact text. Do not copy it into extracted facts.
{% for fact in previous_facts %}
- {{ render_fact(fact, extraction=True) }}
{%- endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif -%}
<|SECTION:{{ summary_target.upper() }}|>
{{ dialogue }}
{% if line_ids %}
Each line starts with its bracketed line id, such as [1043]. The ids are references for the facts list only.
{% endif %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% if summary -%}
<|SECTION:STORED SUMMARY OF {{ summary_target.upper() }}|>
{{ summary }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif -%}
{% include "dynamic-instructions.jinja2" %}
<|SECTION:TASK|>
{% if audience_summary %}
{% include "audience-summary-instructions.jinja2" %}
{% endif -%}
Extract the atomic facts established in {{ summary_target }}.

This is a specific chapter from {{ scene.context }}.
{% if summary %}
The stored summary tells what {{ summary_target }} is about. Use it to understand the chapter. Take every fact from the content of {{ summary_target }} itself. When the summary and the content disagree, the content is correct. A fact the content establishes is valid even when the summary leaves it out. Do not write a new summary.
{% endif %}
{% if extra_context %}Use the previous chapters only to understand the story. Extract only what {{ summary_target }} establishes.
{% endif %}
Your response must be the FACTS block and nothing else:

{% set facts_only = True -%}
{% include "fact-list-instructions.jinja2" %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
